    <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mb-4">Our Verdict</h2>
    <p class="text-gray-400 leading-relaxed">BuyVM is the right pick for developers who want a community-trusted, long-stable KVM VPS host with free DDoS protection and a rare Luxembourg location, and who don't need NVMe storage or 4GB+ RAM on a single plan. The 16-year track record is a real signal — most budget VPS brands we review have been around for 5-10 years, and the steady BuyVM community (LowEndTalk, WebHostingTalk) is rare in this segment. The 3500 Gbps+ DDoS protection included free is the strongest feature for the price, and Anycast IP support is unique. The trade-offs are clear: $2.08/mo gets you 256MB RAM and 30GB SATA — useful for VPN, static sites, and dev sandboxes, but not for databases, large caches, or production app servers. If you need that workload profile, Vultr ($2.50/mo, NVMe, 32 locations) or DigitalOcean ($4/mo, NVMe, managed DBs) are better fits. If you want community-tested KVM with free DDoS, BuyVM is the most credible pick at $2.08/mo.</p>
